<title>JAPAN: IBJ SAYS TO LEAVE AUGUST LONG-TERM PRIME UNCHANGED.</title>
<headline>IBJ SAYS TO LEAVE AUGUST LONG-TERM PRIME UNCHANGED.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd (IBJ) said on Monday it would leave its long-term prime lending rate for August unchanged at 2.7 percent from July.</p>
<p>The bank also said it would set the new coupon rate for its monthly issued five-year debentures for institutional investors at 1.8 percent, unchanged from the July issue.</p>
</text>
